{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have TanStack server tools. A host cannot call those tools over HTTP."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a tool, a resource, and a prompt in one app, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/mcp-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build an MCP Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":" serves those tools over MCP. Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server.fetch(request)"},{"type":"text","value":" from your route."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/mcp-server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nexport const server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the server once. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleMcp"},{"type":"text","value":" calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" for each request."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install these packages:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-mcp\",\"@modelcontextprotocol/server\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save the server code as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/mcp-server.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Forward each request to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleMcp"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/routes/api.mcp.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { handleMcp } from '../mcp-server'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/mcp')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      POST: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      DELETE: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The route path is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/api/mcp"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cloudflare-workers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare Workers"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Save the server code as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/mcp-server.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleMcp"},{"type":"text","value":" for each request."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// src/index.ts\nimport { handleMcp } from './mcp-server'\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request) {\n    return handleMcp(request)\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The worker URL is the MCP URL."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each request can reach a different instance. The server keeps no spec 2025 session by default, so this works with no extra setup. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-sessions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Sessions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":" serves fixed lists of tools, resources, and prompts. It reports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listChanged: false"},{"type":"text","value":" and answers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscriptions/listen"},{"type":"text","value":" with JSON-RPC "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-32601"},{"type":"text","value":". The Worker does not keep an idle subscription stream open."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The host can list "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_weather"},{"type":"text","value":". Then the host can call that tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To call this URL from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/mcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tell-the-host-what-a-tool-does","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tell the host what a tool does"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A host asks the user before it runs a tool, unless the tool says it only reads. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.title"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.annotations"},{"type":"text","value":" on the tool definition. The host gets them as the MCP tool title and annotations."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const listNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'list_notes',\n  description: 'List the notes of the signed-in user',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    title: 'List notes',\n    annotations: { readOnlyHint: true, idempotentHint: true },\n  },\n}).server(async () => [])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The annotation names are the MCP names:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readOnlyHint"},{"type":"text","value":": the tool changes nothing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destructiveHint"},{"type":"text","value":": the tool can delete or overwrite data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idempotentHint"},{"type":"text","value":": a repeat call with the same input changes nothing more."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openWorldHint"},{"type":"text","value":": the tool reaches outside your system."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To show an "},{"type":"link","href":"./apps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Apps"}]},{"type":"text","value":" view for a tool, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata._meta"},{"type":"text","value":". The host gets it as the MCP tool "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_meta"},{"type":"text","value":". The key "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui.resourceUri"},{"type":"text","value":" links the tool to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ui://"},{"type":"text","value":" resource of the view."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const showChart = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'show_chart',\n  description: 'Show the sales chart',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    _meta: { ui: { resourceUri: 'ui://charts/sales' } },\n  },\n}).server(async () => ({ total: 42 }))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"log-sdk-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Log SDK errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some errors never reach your tool code: transport errors, protocol errors, and rejected requests. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onerror"},{"type":"text","value":" to send them to your logs. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serveMCPStdio"},{"type":"text","value":" also sends its transport errors there. It only reports. The response does not change."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  onerror: (error) => console.error('MCP error', error),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"shape-the-result-yourself","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shape the result yourself"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server parses the tool output with its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":". If the output does not match, the call returns a tool error that names the tool. The server sends the output as one text block. An object also goes on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredContent"},{"type":"text","value":". When you want more than one block, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isError"},{"type":"text","value":" without an exception, return an MCP "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CallToolResult"},{"type":"text","value":" from a tool with no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":". The server sends it as is."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const countNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'count_notes',\n  description: 'Count the notes and list them',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n}).server(async () => {\n  const notes = await db.notes.list()\n  return {\n    content: [\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: `${notes.length} notes.` },\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: JSON.stringify(notes) },\n    ],\n    structuredContent: { count: notes.length },\n  }\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first block is a short summary for the model. The second block is the data."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"call-the-server-with-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call the server with types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your app calls the deployed server. You want a wrong tool name or a wrong argument to fail at compile time."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Export "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/mcp-server.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the app, import its type with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import type"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typeof server"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPClient"},{"type":"text","value":", with the URL of the server."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// app/weather.ts\nimport { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport type { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nexport async function forecast(city: string) {\n  const client = await createMCPClient<typeof server>({\n    transport: { type: 'http', url: 'https://mcp.example.com/api/mcp' },\n  })\n  try {\n    return await client.callTool('get_weather', { city })\n  } finally {\n    await client.close()\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client connects to the URL and speaks MCP. The server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth"},{"type":"text","value":" option runs, the same as for any host."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callTool"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts only the tool names of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"},{"type":"text","value":", and each tool's input type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callTool"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the MCP result. For a tool with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredContent"},{"type":"text","value":" has the tool output type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPrompt"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts only the prompt names of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"},{"type":"text","value":", and each prompt's argument type."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readResource"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts only the resource URIs of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"import type"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the server code out of the app bundle."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"call-the-server-in-the-same-process","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call the server in the same process"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the app and the server run in one process, pass the server object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nconst client = await createMCPClient({ server })\nconst text = await client.callTool('get_weather', { city: 'Paris' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This client opens no connection. It calls the tool function directly and returns the tool output."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth"},{"type":"text","value":" option does not run."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools()"},{"type":"text","value":", so you cannot pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool gets the spec 2026 context. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" throws, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" option of the server."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callTool"},{"type":"text","value":" parses the output with the tool "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":", the same as the HTTP server."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readResource(uri, context)"},{"type":"text","value":" puts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" on the resource "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context"},{"type":"text","value":". Without it, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callTool('get_weather', { city })"},{"type":"text","value":" goes to the deployed server, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callTool('get_wether', { city })"},{"type":"text","value":" fails the type check."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the host starts a local process, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-stdio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server on stdio"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"tanstack-start","text":"TanStack Start","level":2},{"id":"cloudflare-workers","text":"Cloudflare Workers","level":2},{"id":"tell-the-host-what-a-tool-does","text":"Tell the host what a tool does","level":2},{"id":"log-sdk-errors","text":"Log SDK errors","level":2},{"id":"shape-the-result-yourself","text":"Shape the result yourself","level":2},{"id":"call-the-server-with-types","text":"Call the server with types","level":2},{"id":"call-the-server-in-the-same-process","text":"Call the server in the same process","level":3}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have TanStack server tools. A host cannot call those tools over HTTP.\n\nFor a tool, a resource, and a prompt in one app, open [Build an MCP Server](../tutorials/mcp-server).\n\n`createMCPServer` serves those tools over MCP. Return `server.fetch(request)` from your route.\n\n```ts\n// src/mcp-server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nexport const server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\nCreate the server once. `handleMcp` calls `fetch` for each request.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall these packages:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nvue: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\npreact: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nangular: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\noctane: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## TanStack Start\n\n1. Save the server code as `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. Forward each request to `handleMcp`.\n\n```ts ignore\n// src/routes/api.mcp.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { handleMcp } from '../mcp-server'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/mcp')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      POST: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      DELETE: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe route path is `/api/mcp`.\n\n## Cloudflare Workers\n\n1. Save the server code as `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. Call `handleMcp` for each request.\n\n```ts\n// src/index.ts\nimport { handleMcp } from './mcp-server'\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request) {\n    return handleMcp(request)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe worker URL is the MCP URL.\n\nEach request can reach a different instance. The server keeps no spec 2025 session by default, so this works with no extra setup. See [MCP Server Sessions](./server-sessions).\n\n`createMCPServer` serves fixed lists of tools, resources, and prompts. It reports `listChanged: false` and answers `subscriptions/listen` with JSON-RPC `-32601`. The Worker does not keep an idle subscription stream open.\n\nThe host can list `get_weather`. Then the host can call that tool.\n\nTo call this URL from `chat()`, see [MCP Server Tools](../tools/mcp).\n\n## Tell the host what a tool does\n\nA host asks the user before it runs a tool, unless the tool says it only reads. Set `metadata.title` and `metadata.annotations` on the tool definition. The host gets them as the MCP tool title and annotations.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const listNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'list_notes',\n  description: 'List the notes of the signed-in user',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    title: 'List notes',\n    annotations: { readOnlyHint: true, idempotentHint: true },\n  },\n}).server(async () => [])\n```\n\nThe annotation names are the MCP names:\n\n- `readOnlyHint`: the tool changes nothing.\n- `destructiveHint`: the tool can delete or overwrite data.\n- `idempotentHint`: a repeat call with the same input changes nothing more.\n- `openWorldHint`: the tool reaches outside your system.\n\nTo show an [MCP Apps](./apps) view for a tool, set `metadata._meta`. The host gets it as the MCP tool `_meta`. The key `ui.resourceUri` links the tool to the `ui://` resource of the view.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const showChart = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'show_chart',\n  description: 'Show the sales chart',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    _meta: { ui: { resourceUri: 'ui://charts/sales' } },\n  },\n}).server(async () => ({ total: 42 }))\n```\n\n## Log SDK errors\n\nSome errors never reach your tool code: transport errors, protocol errors, and rejected requests. Pass `onerror` to send them to your logs. `serveMCPStdio` also sends its transport errors there. It only reports. The response does not change.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  onerror: (error) => console.error('MCP error', error),\n})\n```\n\n## Shape the result yourself\n\nThe server parses the tool output with its `outputSchema`. If the output does not match, the call returns a tool error that names the tool. The server sends the output as one text block. An object also goes on `structuredContent`. When you want more than one block, or `isError` without an exception, return an MCP `CallToolResult` from a tool with no `outputSchema`. The server sends it as is.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const countNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'count_notes',\n  description: 'Count the notes and list them',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n}).server(async () => {\n  const notes = await db.notes.list()\n  return {\n    content: [\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: `${notes.length} notes.` },\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: JSON.stringify(notes) },\n    ],\n    structuredContent: { count: notes.length },\n  }\n})\n```\n\nThe first block is a short summary for the model. The second block is the data.\n\n## Call the server with types\n\nYour app calls the deployed server. You want a wrong tool name or a wrong argument to fail at compile time.\n\n1. Export `server` from `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. In the app, import its type with `import type`.\n3. Pass `typeof server` to `createMCPClient`, with the URL of the server.\n\n```ts\n// app/weather.ts\nimport { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport type { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nexport async function forecast(city: string) {\n  const client = await createMCPClient<typeof server>({\n    transport: { type: 'http', url: 'https://mcp.example.com/api/mcp' },\n  })\n  try {\n    return await client.callTool('get_weather', { city })\n  } finally {\n    await client.close()\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe client connects to the URL and speaks MCP. The server `auth` option runs, the same as for any host.\n\n- `callTool` accepts only the tool names of `server`, and each tool's input type.\n- `callTool` returns the MCP result. For a tool with an `outputSchema`, `structuredContent` has the tool output type.\n- `getPrompt` accepts only the prompt names of `server`, and each prompt's argument type.\n- `readResource` accepts only the resource URIs of `server`.\n- `import type` keeps the server code out of the app bundle.\n\n### Call the server in the same process\n\nWhen the app and the server run in one process, pass the server object:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nconst client = await createMCPClient({ server })\nconst text = await client.callTool('get_weather', { city: 'Paris' })\n```\n\nThis client opens no connection. It calls the tool function directly and returns the tool output.\n\n- The server `auth` option does not run.\n- The client has no `tools()`, so you cannot pass it to `chat()`.\n- A tool gets the spec 2026 context. `ctx.context.requestInput` throws, and `ctx.context.sample` uses the `sample` option of the server.\n- `callTool` parses the output with the tool `outputSchema`, the same as the HTTP server.\n- `readResource(uri, context)` puts `context` on the resource `ctx.context`. Without it, `ctx.context` is `{}`.\n\nNow `callTool('get_weather', { city })` goes to the deployed server, and `callTool('get_wether', { city })` fails the type check.\n\nIf the host starts a local process, see [MCP Server on stdio](./server-stdio).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Serve Tools over HTTP\nid: mcp-server\norder: 13\ndescription: \"Serve TanStack tools over HTTP with createMCPServer so a host can call them.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - mcp server\n  - createMCPServer\n  - tanstack start\n  - cloudflare workers\n---\n\nYou have TanStack server tools. A host cannot call those tools over HTTP.\n\nFor a tool, a resource, and a prompt in one app, open [Build an MCP Server](../tutorials/mcp-server).\n\n`createMCPServer` serves those tools over MCP. Return `server.fetch(request)` from your route.\n\n```ts\n// src/mcp-server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nexport const server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nexport function handleMcp(request: Request) {\n  return server.fetch(request)\n}\n```\n\nCreate the server once. `handleMcp` calls `fetch` for each request.\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall these packages:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nvue: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\npreact: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nangular: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\noctane: @tanstack/ai-mcp @modelcontextprotocol/server\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## TanStack Start\n\n1. Save the server code as `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. Forward each request to `handleMcp`.\n\n```ts ignore\n// src/routes/api.mcp.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { handleMcp } from '../mcp-server'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/mcp')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      POST: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n      DELETE: ({ request }) => handleMcp(request),\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe route path is `/api/mcp`.\n\n## Cloudflare Workers\n\n1. Save the server code as `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. Call `handleMcp` for each request.\n\n```ts\n// src/index.ts\nimport { handleMcp } from './mcp-server'\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request) {\n    return handleMcp(request)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nThe worker URL is the MCP URL.\n\nEach request can reach a different instance. The server keeps no spec 2025 session by default, so this works with no extra setup. See [MCP Server Sessions](./server-sessions).\n\n`createMCPServer` serves fixed lists of tools, resources, and prompts. It reports `listChanged: false` and answers `subscriptions/listen` with JSON-RPC `-32601`. The Worker does not keep an idle subscription stream open.\n\nThe host can list `get_weather`. Then the host can call that tool.\n\nTo call this URL from `chat()`, see [MCP Server Tools](../tools/mcp).\n\n## Tell the host what a tool does\n\nA host asks the user before it runs a tool, unless the tool says it only reads. Set `metadata.title` and `metadata.annotations` on the tool definition. The host gets them as the MCP tool title and annotations.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const listNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'list_notes',\n  description: 'List the notes of the signed-in user',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    title: 'List notes',\n    annotations: { readOnlyHint: true, idempotentHint: true },\n  },\n}).server(async () => [])\n```\n\nThe annotation names are the MCP names:\n\n- `readOnlyHint`: the tool changes nothing.\n- `destructiveHint`: the tool can delete or overwrite data.\n- `idempotentHint`: a repeat call with the same input changes nothing more.\n- `openWorldHint`: the tool reaches outside your system.\n\nTo show an [MCP Apps](./apps) view for a tool, set `metadata._meta`. The host gets it as the MCP tool `_meta`. The key `ui.resourceUri` links the tool to the `ui://` resource of the view.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport const showChart = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'show_chart',\n  description: 'Show the sales chart',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n  metadata: {\n    _meta: { ui: { resourceUri: 'ui://charts/sales' } },\n  },\n}).server(async () => ({ total: 42 }))\n```\n\n## Log SDK errors\n\nSome errors never reach your tool code: transport errors, protocol errors, and rejected requests. Pass `onerror` to send them to your logs. `serveMCPStdio` also sends its transport errors there. It only reports. The response does not change.\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  onerror: (error) => console.error('MCP error', error),\n})\n```\n\n## Shape the result yourself\n\nThe server parses the tool output with its `outputSchema`. If the output does not match, the call returns a tool error that names the tool. The server sends the output as one text block. An object also goes on `structuredContent`. When you want more than one block, or `isError` without an exception, return an MCP `CallToolResult` from a tool with no `outputSchema`. The server sends it as is.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nexport const countNotes = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'count_notes',\n  description: 'Count the notes and list them',\n  inputSchema: z.object({}),\n}).server(async () => {\n  const notes = await db.notes.list()\n  return {\n    content: [\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: `${notes.length} notes.` },\n      { type: 'text' as const, text: JSON.stringify(notes) },\n    ],\n    structuredContent: { count: notes.length },\n  }\n})\n```\n\nThe first block is a short summary for the model. The second block is the data.\n\n## Call the server with types\n\nYour app calls the deployed server. You want a wrong tool name or a wrong argument to fail at compile time.\n\n1. Export `server` from `src/mcp-server.ts`.\n2. In the app, import its type with `import type`.\n3. Pass `typeof server` to `createMCPClient`, with the URL of the server.\n\n```ts\n// app/weather.ts\nimport { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport type { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nexport async function forecast(city: string) {\n  const client = await createMCPClient<typeof server>({\n    transport: { type: 'http', url: 'https://mcp.example.com/api/mcp' },\n  })\n  try {\n    return await client.callTool('get_weather', { city })\n  } finally {\n    await client.close()\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe client connects to the URL and speaks MCP. The server `auth` option runs, the same as for any host.\n\n- `callTool` accepts only the tool names of `server`, and each tool's input type.\n- `callTool` returns the MCP result. For a tool with an `outputSchema`, `structuredContent` has the tool output type.\n- `getPrompt` accepts only the prompt names of `server`, and each prompt's argument type.\n- `readResource` accepts only the resource URIs of `server`.\n- `import type` keeps the server code out of the app bundle.\n\n### Call the server in the same process\n\nWhen the app and the server run in one process, pass the server object:\n\n```ts\nimport { createMCPClient } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp'\nimport { server } from '../src/mcp-server'\n\nconst client = await createMCPClient({ server })\nconst text = await client.callTool('get_weather', { city: 'Paris' })\n```\n\nThis client opens no connection. It calls the tool function directly and returns the tool output.\n\n- The server `auth` option does not run.\n- The client has no `tools()`, so you cannot pass it to `chat()`.\n- A tool gets the spec 2026 context. `ctx.context.requestInput` throws, and `ctx.context.sample` uses the `sample` option of the server.\n- `callTool` parses the output with the tool `outputSchema`, the same as the HTTP server.\n- `readResource(uri, context)` puts `context` on the resource `ctx.context`. Without it, `ctx.context` is `{}`.\n\nNow `callTool('get_weather', { city })` goes to the deployed server, and `callTool('get_wether', { city })` fails the type check.\n\nIf the host starts a local process, see [MCP Server on stdio](./server-stdio).\n"}
